We walk into the small cafeteria in the hall.
We find a table.
I am very thirsty.
We drink cold water and talk.
"This is a really good club," I say.
"It is a good sport to do," Kasper says.
Kasper looks at me.
"Do you want to join again?" he asks.
"Yes, very much," I answer.
"I want to play here every Thursday," I explain.
"That sounds lovely," Sara says.
"We always play here on Thursdays," Kasper says.
"Then we'll see each other next week," I say happily.
We drink the rest of our water.
It is lovely to meet new people.
